cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these examples, please cite them as below."
type: software
title: "Corleone.jl: examples and benchmarks"
abstract: >-
  Example scripts, pinned Julia environment, and benchmark results for
  Corleone.jl v2.1.0: optimal control of the Lotka-Volterra fishing problem
  with single and multiple shooting and integer controls, a universal
  differential equation trained with CorleoneInverse.jl, and optimal
  experimental design with CorleoneOED.jl.
version: v1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/mathopt/Corleone-Paper-Examples
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24551106
keywords:
  - Julia
  - optimal control
  - multiple shooting
  - scientific machine learning
  - optimal experimental design
authors:
  - {given-names: Carl Julius, family-names: Martensen, affiliation: "Otto von Guericke University Magdeburg"}
  - {given-names: Christoph, family-names: Plate, affiliation: "Max Planck Institute for Dynamics of Complex Technical Systems"}
  - {given-names: Christian, family-names: Kirches, affiliation: "Braunschweig University of Technology"}
  - {given-names: Andreas, family-names: Potschka, affiliation: "Clausthal University of Technology"}
  - {given-names: Christopher Vincent, family-names: Rackauckas, affiliation: "Massachusetts Institute of Technology"}
  - {given-names: Sebastian, family-names: Sager, affiliation: "Otto von Guericke University Magdeburg"}
